AArch64 MP+caspal-arr+ldp
"CASPAL (0,0)->(1,2) on two 8-byte array elements vs LDP: on FEAT_LSE2 hardware both are 16-byte single-copy atomic (aligned), so no torn read"
{
uint64_t t[2];
0:X4=t; 1:X4=t;
uint64_t 0:X0; uint64_t 0:X1; uint64_t 1:X7; uint64_t 1:X8;
}
 P0                      | P1             ;
 MOV X0,#0               | LDP X7,X8,[X4] ;
 MOV X1,#0               |                ;
 MOV X2,#1               |                ;
 MOV X3,#2               |                ;
 CASPAL X0,X1,X2,X3,[X4] |                ;
exists (1:X7=1 /\ 1:X8=0 \/ 1:X7=0 /\ 1:X8=2)
